---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Resources"
  description="Whitepaper, developer docs, public RFCs, and research for SensOS."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Resources</p>
    <h1>Evaluate SensOS with the right depth</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Public materials explain value and interfaces. Implementation detail stays
      behind enterprise and partner access.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="home-block" id="whitepaper">
    <h2>Whitepaper</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Observation First: Runtime Safety Without Changing Your Model.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      Executive brief for CIO/CISO/CTO audiences covering the black-box gap,
      observation-centered control, and open-standards interoperability.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Full PDF packaging in progress — request via Enterprise.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/enterprise#demo">Request Whitepaper</a>
  </section>

  <section class="home-block">
    <h2>Developer Docs</h2>
    <p>Integrate against public contracts and conformance tiers.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/developer">Open Developer Docs</a>
  </section>

  <section class="home-block">
    <h2>Open Standards</h2>
    <p>
      Charter, public RFCs, conformance, and certification.
      Interface standards — not implementation manuals.
    </p>
    <a class="btn" href="/Open-Standards">Open Standards</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/Open-Standards/RFCs">Public RFCs</a>
  </section>

  <section class="home-block" id="case-studies">
    <h2>Case Studies</h2>
    <p>Production patterns for AI platform and risk teams (coming soon).</p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-block" id="research">
    <h2>Research</h2>
    <p>
      Selected public notes and mathematical interface contracts.
      Tuned formulas and calibration remain unpublished.
    </p>
    <a class="btn" href="/rfc">View Public Standards</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .home-block {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .home-block h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .home-block p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .muted {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
